        "original_id": "f783889d-5922-5d23-ba56-ba2a8b4b16ac",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Juniper, Indigofera\n- Taxonomy: Juniperus, Cupressaceae, Fabaceae\n- Places: James Wild Horse Trap\n- Compounds: Indican\n\nFacts:\n- Junipers are coniferous plants in the genus Juniperus of the cypress family Cupressaceae.\n- Indigofera is a large genus of more than 750 species of flowering plants in the family Fabaceae.\n- James Wild Horse Trap was the location of a corral and fences used to capture wild horses, and those structures were built from dead juniper trees.\n- Indican is a colorless organic compound that is soluble in water and occurs naturally in Indigofera plants.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
