        "text": "Page: Juniper. Sentence: Junipers are coniferous plants in the genus Juniperus of the cypress family Cupressaceae.\nPage: Indigofera. Sentence: Indigofera is a large genus of over 750 species of flowering plants belonging to the family Fabaceae.\nPage: James Wild Horse Trap. Sentence: It was the location of a corral and fences used to capture wild horses, built out of dead Juniper trees.\nPage: Indican. Sentence: Indican is a colourless organic compound, soluble in water, naturally occurring in \"Indigofera\" plants.",
